values ('c4e8a1b2-7f03-4d6e-8a91-2b5c0e9d4f18', 'chemistry-for-health-sciences', 'Chemistry for Health Sciences', 'Chemistry for Health Sciences is a general, organic, and biological chemistry course for nursing and allied-health students. It builds measurement and dose-style quantitative habits, then covers atoms, bonding, reactions, body fluids, pH and buffers, functional groups, stereochemistry, biomolecules, metabolism, clinical chemistry, and laboratory data literacy. The course keeps a nursing-focused GOB spine while adding clinical and biochemical context for later anatomy, physiology, pharmacology, pathophysiology, and nutrition.');

